===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[appliance]] or [[room]] used to [[store]] food or other [[perishable]] [[item]]s at [[temperature]]s below 0[[°]] [[Celsius]] (32° [[Fahrenheit]]).
#: {{hypo|en|chest freezer|deep freeze|deep freezer|deep-freezer<qq:stand-alone appliance>|;|cooler<qq:room>|walk-in<qq:room>}}
#: {{cot|en|fridge|refrigerator|;|icebox}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976 |title=USITC Publication - Issue 773  |author=|page=A-33 |ISBN=|passage=The packinghouse usually delivers shrimp to a few regular customers, such as breaders, '''freezers''', canners, or wholesalers of fresh shrimp.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Tejal Rao|title=Making Mochi, a Japanese Treat That’s All About Texture|work=w:The New York Times|date=2016-06-27|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/06/29/dining/mochi-recipe-tomoko-kato.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=It’s easy to grab plastic-wrapped daifuku at Japanese grocery stores in New York, and to spot boxes of mochi ice cream in supermarket '''freezer''' aisles.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=w:The Guardian|title=Man caught fly-tipping fridge in ravine fined and made to drag it back|author=Stephen Burgen|date=2019-08-06
|passage=Fridges contain gases that can cause serious environmental damage and are among the most toxic white goods if not disposed of correctly, along with '''freezers''' and air conditioning units.
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2019/aug/06/man-caught-fly-tipping-fridge-in-ravine-fined-and-made-to-drag-back}}
# The [[section]] of a [[refrigerator]] used to store food or other perishable items at a temperature below 0[[°]] [[Celsius]] (32° [[Fahrenheit]]).
#: {{hyper|en|compartment}}
#: {{hol|en|fridge|fridge-freezer|refrigerator|refrigerator-freezer}}
# {{lb|en|neuroscience|[[Parkinson's disease]]}} A [[Parkinson's disease]] patient that experiences ''freezing of gait'' (FOG) episodes.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[hardware]] [[device]] that can [[freeze]] the state of the [[system]] to allow it to be inspected, saved or modified.
#* ''Early Home Computers'' (page 231)
#*: {{...}} "'''freezer'''" cartridges (such as the Action Replay), as a convenient way to take control {{...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2016|author=Polgár Tamás|title=Freax: The Brief History of the Computer Demoscene
|passage=The execution of the program was suspended with a special hardware expansion, ''the '''freezer''''', and the contents of the memory were saved to disk.}}

